What is High Pressure Laminate?
High Pressure Laminate (HPL) is a multi layer composite material that combines layers of cellulose paper, phenolic resin, and a melamine formaldehyde overlay, all fused together under high temperature and pressure. The process yields a single, rigid sheet that offers exceptional scratch resistance, moisture tolerance, and dimensional stability. These inherent properties make HPL an attractive choice for a broad spectrum of applications, from kitchen countertops and bathroom vanities to wall panels, flooring, furniture facings, and architectural façade elements.
